From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:15:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: rx lengths, PS and TWT locking, debugfs,
 teardown order

rx (mt7915_mac_fill_rx):
- the global wcid (WTBL entry 0) and an interface's entry are no
  station's: no poll, no 802.11 header rebuilt for them;
- an 802.11 frame needs all of its header (ieee80211_hdrlen()) before
  a CCMP header goes in behind it and its fields are read;
- the C-RXV is copied before a fragment's rebuilt header goes over it,
  as the HE radiotap fields are read from it afterwards.

Power save and TWT:
- the PS record's lock is initialised for a new station only, not
  again when mac80211 re-adds it after a full reset;
- the firmware's doze events and a TWT agreement's start or end decide
  the hold under that lock;
- the L1 recovery's release too.
- TWT policy: suggested terms are the policy's fixed point (the TU-mode
  floor capped at what 63 TUs hold; the interval nearest the limits, one
  fixed fallback where none fits), so a device taking them up gets them
  accepted;
- new terms for a flow a station has don't count it twice against the
  limits, and the old flow stays when they are refused.

debugfs:
- fw_debug_bin's channel is opened, reset (unpublished meanwhile) and
  closed under one mutex;
- a log event shorter than its magic isn't a binary log;
- the readers and writers that touch WFSYS registers or the MCU take
  the device mutex (hw-queues and the stations' queues share
  MT_FL_Q0_CTRL);
- fixed_rate's bandwidth is checked (its parsing split out);
- twt_policy takes decimal numbers only;
- twt_teardown checks its words first and looks the station up under
  RCU;
- ps reads silent_ms before the flag.

Teardown and errors:
- mt7915_unregister_hw() is all of mt7915_unregister_device() but the
  free, so the MT798x platform driver frees its interrupt in between;
- the handler leaves the registers alone once mt7915_stop_hardware()
  has powered WFSYS down;
- an MCU timeout queues the reset only once the hardware is up;
- a registration failing late sets MT76_REMOVED and cancels the
  reset/dump/rc work;
- set_vow_band is sent under the mutex in add_interface.

KUnit for each, two on a second CPU (the re-add, the TWT update), and
the fails-before checks done with mutants.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
